# Lychee link-checker ignore file.
#
# Each non-comment line is a Rust regex matched against the full URL
# (scheme + host + path + fragment). A URL is skipped if the regex
# matches its host OR its path. Comments start with `#`.
#
# The validation workflow and `scripts/validate-local.sh` run lychee
# against `**/*.{md,ts,svelte}` with `--offline`. Use this file for
# URL / host patterns; pass file-system exclusions via
# `--exclude-path` in the workflow instead, because file globs are
# not valid URL regexes (they cause "repetition operator missing
# expression" errors).
#
# Localhost / loopback hosts.
^https?://(localhost|127\.0\.0\.1|0\.0\.0\.0|\[::1\])(:\d+)?(/|$)

# Mailto links cannot be checked offline.
^mailto:

# file:// URLs are not reachable from the runner.
^file://

# Same-page anchors (Markdown heading links).
#
# Lychee reports `#fragment` as a separate link; ignore them.
^[^/]+#.*
